          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+Artinian+local+ring"} ordered Artinian local ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_+
            are a subset of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:\mathbb{Z}_+ \hookrightarrow R
            %strong Archimedean ordered Artinian local ring
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+Artinian+local+ring"} ordered Artinian local ring
            which satisfies the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+property"} archimedean property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in R
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt a
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}_+
            such that such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt i(n) \cdot b
          %p
            Archimedean ordered Artinian local rings are important because they are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+local+rings"} ordered local rings
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent"} nilpotent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimals"} infinitesimals
            but no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+elements"} infinite elements
            or invertible infinitesimals, and thus play an important role in synthetic approaches to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+fields"} Archimedean ordered fields
            are the Archimedean ordered Artinian local rings in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilradical"} nilradical
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial"} trivial ideal
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#purely_real_and_purely_infinitesimal_elements Purely real and purely infinitesimal elements
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+field"} Archimedean ordered field
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an Archimedean ordered Artinian local
            = succeed "-algebra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            by its ideal of non-invertible elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            itself, and the canonical function used in defining the quotient is the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re:A \to K
            which takes a number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            to its purely real component
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re(a) \in K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an ordered
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strictly+monotone"} strictly monotone
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:K \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            is
            %strong purely real
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(\Re(a)) = a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            is
            %strong
              purely
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal"} infinitesimal
            if it is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            which is both purely real and purely infinitesimal.
